{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792611723,"nonce":"HbqWfUASPMI5TQuYLhLKZVN89T4=","title":"An Environment's `approvers` are enforced ONLY inside the manual-gate approval path: `approve_gate` checks `r.admits(\u0026c.git_ref, \u0026approvers)` (crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs ~6552-6567). Nothing found (by search — not proof of absence) forces a Deploy Run into a protected Environment to contain a manual gate. So a pipeline with `environment: prod` and NO `gate:` step is never asked for approval: prod approvers are opt-in by the pipeline author, contradicting ADR-0037's \"the environment governs regardless of what the YAML says\".","message":"Fix direction: at Run creation (where allowed_refs/require_reason are already enforced, ~lib.rs:3937-3960), if the Environment has approvers, either reject a Deploy Run with no manual gate fronting the deploy steps, or have the engine inject an implicit approval gate before the first step. Decide which; injecting matches \"governs regardless of YAML\".\nAcceptance: a Deploy Run into an Environment with approvers and no authored gate cannot run any step until the approvers approve (or is rejected at creation); a test proves it.\nFound by the 2026-10-22 deployments/plugins design audit (independent judge), verified by hand.","files":null}]}